@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il28-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 48A and the Income Tax (Credits for a Foreign Worker)
-- Regulations, 5775-2014, with the Foreign Workers Law 5751-1991 s 1 for the
-- definition of a foreign worker. Row IL-28.
--
-- s 48A is a power: the Minister of Finance may determine that the credit
-- provisions of Chapter Three of Part C "do not apply to a foreign worker, or to
-- classes of foreign workers he determines, or apply to them partially on
-- conditions he determines", ”אף אם רואים אותו כתושב לענין פקודה זו“. The
-- Regulations (four regulations) are what he determined: reg 3 gives a legal
-- foreign worker a few credit points and takes every other provision of the
-- chapter away; reg 4 starts them with income produced in the 2015 tax year.
--
-- Source quotations below are generated from the deposited files by
-- tools/srcquote.py and checked line by line by tools/hebcheck.py.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 48A and the Regulations of 5775-2014`

§§ `Section 48A — the power`

-- src:ITO:1810 | סעיף 48א – זיכויים לעובד זר [תיקון: תשס״ג־3]
-- src:ITO:1811 | שר האוצר רשאי לקבוע כי הוראות פרק זה לענין זיכויים, כולן או מקצתן, לא יחולו על עובד זר או על סוגי עובדים זרים שיקבע, או שיחולו עליהם באופן חלקי בתנאים שיקבע; לענין זה, ”עובד זר“ – כהגדרתו בחוק עובדים זרים (איסור העסקה שלא כדין והבטחת תנאים הוגנים), התשנ״א–1991, אף אם רואים אותו כתושב לענין פקודה זו.
-- src:ITO:1812 | [note: פורסמו תקנות מס הכנסה (זיכויים לעובד זר), התשע״ה–2014.]

§§ `Who is a foreign worker`

-- The Foreign Workers Law's definition, which s 48A adopts.
-- src:FWL:34 | ”עובד זר“ – עובד שאינו אזרח ישראל, או תושב בה;

-- The Regulations narrow it: a foreign worker for their purposes holds, or needs, a visa under s 2 of the Entry into
-- Israel Law.
-- src:REG:17 | ”עובד זר“ – כהגדרתו בסעיף 48א לפקודה שהוא בעל אשרה לפי סעיף 2 לחוק הכניסה לישראל, התשי״ב–1952, או ששהייתו או העסקתו בישראל טעונה אשרה כאמור;

@ref FWL s 1, line 34
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the taxpayer is a foreign worker within section 48A` t MEANS
        t's `an individual`
    AND t's `a worker`
    AND NOT t's `an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`
    AND NOT t's `a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`

-- Note that nothing here asks whether the worker is an Israeli resident for income tax: s 48A says ”אף אם רואים אותו
-- כתושב לענין פקודה זו“, so a foreign worker who counts as an Israeli resident under s 1 is still one.
@ref REG 1, line 17
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Regulations reach the taxpayer as a foreign worker` t MEANS
        `the taxpayer is a foreign worker within section 48A` t
    AND t's `holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one`

-- src:REG:24 | עובד זר חוקי הוא עובד זר שהתקיימו בו כל אלה:
-- src:REG:25 | (1) שהייתו בישראל או באזור והעסקתו בישראל או באזור מותרות לפי דין;
-- src:REG:26 | (2) הוא אינו ”מומחה חוץ“ או ”מרצה אורח“ כהגדרתם בתקנות ניכוי הוצאות שהייה;
-- src:REG:27 | (3) הוא קיבל אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ביקור מסוג ב/1 (עובד זמני) לעבודה בישראל, כאמור בתקנה 5(א) לתקנות הכניסה לישראל, התשל״ד–1974.

@ref REG 2, lines 24-27
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker` t MEANS
        `the Regulations reach the taxpayer as a foreign worker` t
    AND t's `stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law`
    AND NOT t's `an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`
    AND t's `holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`

-- src:REG:19 | ”עובד זר חוקי בתחום הסיעוד“ – עובד זר חוקי, שקיבל היתר לעסוק בתחום הסיעוד, ושהארכת שהייתו בישראל מתבצעת לפי סעיף 3א(ב) לחוק הכניסה לישראל, התשי״ב–1952;

@ref REG 1, line 19
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker in the caring sector` t MEANS
        `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker` t
    AND t's `holds a permit to work in the caring sector`
    AND t's `the stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law`

§§ `The tax years the Regulations govern`

-- src:REG:37 | תקנות אלה יחולו בחישוב המס על הכנסתו של עובד זר שהופקה בשנת המס 2015 או לאחריה.

-- REG 4 starts the Regulations with income produced in the 2015 tax year. The Regulations were amended twice
-- (the heading of reg 3 lists תשע״ז and תשע״ח, K.T. 5777 p. 472 and 5778 p. 2656), and the deposited text is the
-- consolidation at retrieval, with neither amending instrument deposited. As row IL-01 does (its fork F12), the
-- deposited text governs a tax year that begins after the Hebrew year of its last listed amendment has ended:
-- 5778 ended 9 September 2018, so 2019. The tax years 2015 to 2018 need the Regulations as made (K.T. 5775 p. 14)
-- and as first amended. The numbers in the Regulations, a few credit points, have not been checked against those.
-- ASSUMED, not ruled: the choice of 2019, from IL-01's F12 (the lead's choice).

@ref REG 3 heading, line 29; REG 4, line 37
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding holds the Regulations as they stood only from the tax year 2019` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding holds the Regulations as they stood only from the tax year 2019"

@ref ITO s 48A, line 1810 (amendment תשס״ג־3); REG 4, line 37; fork FW2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Regulations start with the tax year 2015 and whether an instrument under section 48A applied from 2002 to 2014 is not in the sources` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Regulations start with the tax year 2015 and whether an instrument under section 48A applied from 2002 to 2014 is not in the sources"

-- TRUE: the Regulations govern the tax year. FALSE: they do not and, s 48A's power having produced nothing for that
-- year, the ordinary sections govern. Before 2002 s 48A did not exist (row IL-01, fork F13: the first tax year its
-- enactment in 5763 could reach is 2002).
@ref ITO s 48A line 1810; REG 4 line 37; fork FW2
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Regulations govern the tax year of` t `, under` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF t's `the tax year` LESS THAN 2002 THEN FALSE
           IF t's `the tax year` LESS THAN 2015
               THEN CONSIDER r's `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`
                    WHEN `no instrument under section 48A applied before the regulations of 5775-2014` THEN FALSE
                    WHEN `declined for the tax years from 2002 to 2014`
                        THEN `the Regulations start with the tax year 2015 and whether an instrument under section 48A applied from 2002 to 2014 is not in the sources`
           IF t's `the tax year` LESS THAN 2019 THEN `this encoding holds the Regulations as they stood only from the tax year 2019`
           OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Regulation 3 — the credits`

-- src:REG:30 | (א) בחישוב המס על הכנסה של עובד זר חוקי בתחום הסיעוד, לפי סעיף 2(1) או (2) לפקודה, יובאו בחשבון נקודות זיכוי לפי סעיפים 34, 36 ו־36א לפקודה.
-- src:REG:31 | (א1) בחישוב המס על הכנסה לפי סעיף 2(1) או (2) לפקודה של עובד זר חוקי שאינו עובד זר חוקי בתחום הסיעוד, תובא בחשבון נקודת זיכוי לפי סעיף 34 לפקודה.
-- src:REG:32 | (ב) בחישוב המס על הכנסה לפי סעיף 2(1) או (2) לפקודה של עובדת זרה חוקית שאינה עובדת זרה חוקית בתחום הסיעוד, תובא בחשבון חצי נקודת זיכוי לפי סעיף 36א לפקודה.
-- src:REG:33 | (ג) שהה העובד הזר החוקי או העובד הזר החוקי בתחום הסיעוד, לפי העניין, בישראל או באזור בחלק משנת המס, יובא בחשבון בחישוב המס על הכנסתו, החלק השנים עשר מסכום נקודות הזיכוי כאמור בסעיפים קטנים (א) עד (ב), לפי העניין, כשהוא מוכפל במספר החודשים שבהם שהה בארץ בשנת המס.
-- src:REG:34 | (ד) הוראות הפרק השלישי לחלק ג׳ לפקודה, למעט האמור בתקנות אלה, לא יחולו בחישוב המס על הכנסתו של עובד זר.

@ref this row; input discipline
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the months spent in Israel or the Area must be a whole number from 0 to 12` MEANS
    REFUSE "the months spent in Israel or the Area must be a whole number from 0 to 12"

@ref REG 3(a)-(b), lines 30-32; fork FW1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident"

@ref ITO s 36, line 1594; fork F2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point"

@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; fork F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point"

-- REG 3(a): a caring-sector legal foreign worker: ss 34, 36 and 36A (2, 1/4, and 1/2 for a woman).
-- REG 3(a1): any other legal foreign worker: one point under s 34.
-- REG 3(b): any other legal foreign woman: half a point under s 36A.
-- All three are "in computing tax on income under s 2(1) or (2)".
-- Whole-year amounts, before the monthly fraction of reg 3(c).

@ref REG 3(a) and (a1), lines 30-31
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole-year amount under section 34 that regulation 3 names for` t MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT t's `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)` THEN 0
           IF `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker in the caring sector` t THEN 2
           IF `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker` t THEN 1
           OTHERWISE 0

@ref REG 3(a), line 30
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole-year amount under section 36 that regulation 3 names for` t MEANS
    IF     t's `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)`
       AND `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker in the caring sector` t
    THEN 1/4
    ELSE 0

@ref REG 3(a) and (b), lines 30 and 32
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole-year amount under section 36A that regulation 3 names for` t MEANS
    IF     t's `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)`
       AND t's `a woman`
       AND `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker` t
    THEN 1/2
    ELSE 0

-- Fork F2 (carried from row IL-01) for the quarter point.
@ref ITO s 36, line 1594; fork F2
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quarter point after fork F2 for` t `, under` r MEANS
    IF t's `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year`
    THEN 1/4
    ELSE CONSIDER r's `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion`
         WHEN `section 36 for every individual` THEN 1/4
         WHEN `section 36 only for an individual with income from personal exertion` THEN 0
         WHEN `declined where income from personal exertion decides section 36`
             THEN `section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point`

-- Fork FW1 for s 34: a foreign worker who is an Israeli resident meets the residence limb on any reading.
@ref REG 3(a), (a1), line 30-31; ITO s 34, line 1570; fork FW1
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole-year points under section 34 for` t `, under` r MEANS
    IF `the whole-year amount under section 34 that regulation 3 names for` t EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF t's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
         THEN `the whole-year amount under section 34 that regulation 3 names for` t
         ELSE CONSIDER r's `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`
              WHEN `the regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions`
                  THEN `the whole-year amount under section 34 that regulation 3 names for` t
              WHEN `the cited sections' own residence conditions still apply` THEN 0
              WHEN `declined where the cited sections' residence conditions decide`
                  THEN `the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident`

@ref REG 3(a), line 30; ITO s 36, line 1594; forks F2 and FW1
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole-year points under section 36 for` t `, under` r MEANS
    IF `the whole-year amount under section 36 that regulation 3 names for` t EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF t's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
         THEN `the quarter point after fork F2 for` t `, under` r
         ELSE CONSIDER r's `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`
              WHEN `the regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions`
                  THEN `the quarter point after fork F2 for` t `, under` r
              WHEN `the cited sections' own residence conditions still apply` THEN 0
              WHEN `declined where the cited sections' residence conditions decide`
                  THEN IF `the quarter point after fork F2 for` t `, under` r EQUALS 0
                       THEN 0
                       ELSE `the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident`

-- s 36A has no residence limb of its own. Under FW1 reading A the Regulations give the half point to a woman;
-- under reading B the section's own condition applies, which is fork F1.
@ref REG 3(a) and (b), lines 30 and 32; ITO s 36A, line 1597; forks F1 and FW1
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole-year points under section 36A for` t `, under` r MEANS
    IF `the whole-year amount under section 36A that regulation 3 names for` t EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF t's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
         THEN 1/2
         ELSE CONSIDER r's `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`
              WHEN `the regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions` THEN 1/2
              WHEN `the cited sections' own residence conditions still apply`
                  THEN CONSIDER r's `fork F1, section 36A and residence`
                       WHEN `section 36A has no residence condition` THEN 1/2
                       WHEN `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident` THEN 0
                       WHEN `declined where residence decides section 36A`
                           THEN `section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point`
              WHEN `declined where the cited sections' residence conditions decide`
                  THEN CONSIDER r's `fork F1, section 36A and residence`
                       WHEN `section 36A has no residence condition` THEN 1/2
                       WHEN `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident`
                           THEN `the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident`
                       WHEN `declined where residence decides section 36A`
                           THEN `the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident`

-- REG 3(c): a foreign worker who stayed in Israel or the Area for part of the tax year gets one twelfth of the points
-- for each month of the stay. For a stay of the whole year (12 months) the factor is 1.
@ref REG 3(c), line 33
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fraction of the year that regulation 3(c) allows for` t MEANS
    IF   t's `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area` LESS THAN 0
      OR t's `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN `the months spent in Israel or the Area must be a whole number from 0 to 12`
    ELSE t's `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area` DIVIDED BY 12

@ref REG 3(a)-(c), lines 30-33; REG 3(d), line 34
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A `Credit points`
`the credit points the Regulations give to` t `, under` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the Regulations reach the taxpayer as a foreign worker` t
               THEN `the Regulations do not reach the taxpayer, so their points are not asked`
           IF NOT `the Regulations govern the tax year of` t `, under` r
               THEN `the Regulations do not govern the tax year, so their points are not asked`
           OTHERWISE `Credit points` WITH
               `the points under section 34`  IS `the whole-year points under section 34 for` t `, under` r TIMES `the fraction of the year that regulation 3(c) allows for` t
               `the points under section 36`  IS `the whole-year points under section 36 for` t `, under` r TIMES `the fraction of the year that regulation 3(c) allows for` t
               `the points under section 36A` IS `the whole-year points under section 36A for` t `, under` r TIMES `the fraction of the year that regulation 3(c) allows for` t
               -- REG 3(d): every other provision of the chapter is disapplied, s 37 among them.
               `the points under section 37`  IS 0

@ref REG 1, line 17
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Regulations do not reach the taxpayer, so their points are not asked` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Regulations do not reach the taxpayer, so their points are not asked"

@ref REG 4, line 37; ITO s 48A, line 1810
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Regulations do not govern the tax year, so their points are not asked` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Regulations do not govern the tax year, so their points are not asked"

§§ `Regulation 3(d) — what happens to the rest of Chapter Three`

@ref REG 3(d), line 34; ITO s 48A, line 1810; fork FW3
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3(d) speaks of the whole chapter but section 48A's power speaks of credits, so whether it reaches the chapter's deductions is not decided` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3(d) speaks of the whole chapter but section 48A's power speaks of credits, so whether it reaches the chapter's deductions is not decided"

-- For a credit section other than 34, 36 and 36A the Regulations disapply it on either reading of fork FW3; for
-- the two deduction sections (47, 47A) the readings differ. For ss 34, 36 and 36A the effect is a partial one: the
-- points above, and none at all to a foreign worker who is not a legal one or whose income is not under s 2(1) or (2).
@ref REG 3(d), line 34; ITO s 48A, line 1810; fork FW3
GIVEN p IS A `A provision of Chapter Three`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A `What an instrument does to a provision`
`what the Regulations do to` p `, under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `section 34`  THEN `gives the provision a partial effect, set out in the points`
    WHEN `section 36`  THEN `gives the provision a partial effect, set out in the points`
    WHEN `section 36A` THEN `gives the provision a partial effect, set out in the points`
    WHEN `section 47, a deduction` THEN `what the Regulations do to a deduction, under` r
    WHEN `section 47A, a deduction` THEN `what the Regulations do to a deduction, under` r
    OTHERWISE `disapplies the provision`

GIVEN r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A `What an instrument does to a provision`
`what the Regulations do to a deduction, under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`
    WHEN `regulation 3(d) reaches the whole chapter as it is written` THEN `disapplies the provision`
    WHEN `regulation 3(d) reaches credits only, which is all the power of section 48A gives` THEN `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`
    WHEN `declined where regulation 3(d) and the chapter's deductions meet`
        THEN `regulation 3(d) speaks of the whole chapter but section 48A's power speaks of credits, so whether it reaches the chapter's deductions is not decided`
